\subsection{Reasoning Loops}
\label{sec:loops}
The degenerate-output rule does not catch reasoning that keeps repeating itself. We count a trace as looping if most of its last 300 words repeat 8-grams from earlier in the same trace. The Claude 3.7 student loops in 142 of its 500 CoT-Control traces; the R1 student almost never does. With looping traces scored as failures, the Claude 3.7 student remains above the R1 student ($+3.98$, $[1.32, 6.81]$).
